algorithms.pseudocode:
function VerifyDecomposition(F, S, w, ε, n_tests):
    // Check representation accuracy
    for i = 1 to n_tests:
        f ← random input
        if |F(f) - tropMax(S, w, f)| > ε: return FAIL

    // Check sup-preservation
    for i = 1 to n_tests:
        f, g ← random inputs
        if |F(max(f,g)) - max(F(f), F(g))| > ε: return FAIL

    // Check shift-equivariance
    for i = 1 to n_tests:
        f ← random input, c ← random scalar
        if |F(f+c) - F(f) - c| > ε: return FAIL

    // Check irredundancy
    for s in S:
        f ← isolation function for s
        if max not uniquely at s: return FAIL

    return PASS

Complexity: O(n_tests × |S| × dim)
